   "versionNonce": 700168,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "acquire(), and the one branch that looks like a bug and is not",
   "originalText": "acquire(), and the one branch that looks like a bug and is not",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "acq",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 616,
   "width": 1000,
   "height": 310,
   "strokeColor": "#1e293b",
   "backgroundColor": "#1e293b",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100025,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700175,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "acq_t",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "acq_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 38,
   "y": 613,
   "width": 984,
   "height": 315,
   "strokeColor": "#ffffff",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100026,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700182,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "DistributedLock.acquire(lockPath):\n    myPath = client.create(lockPath + '/lock-', data=sessionId,\n                           mode=EPHEMERAL_SEQUENTIAL)   # server assigns the number\n\n    while true:\n        children = client.getChildren(lockPath, watch=false)\n        sorted   = sort(children)            # purely numeric on the suffix\n\n        if myPath == sorted[0]:\n            return LockHandle(myPath,\n                              fencingToken=parseSequenceNumber(myPath))\n\n        predecessor = sorted[indexOf(myPath) - 1]   # the ONE node ahead of me\n        watchResult = client.exists(lockPath + '/' + predecessor, watch=true)\n\n        if watchResult is null:\n            continue          # already gone - recheck NOW, do not wait for a\n                              # watch event that will never fire\n\n        waitForWatchEvent()   # ONE-SHOT: fires once, then must be re-set\n        # loop: re-list children, re-check whether I am now lowest",
   "originalText": "DistributedLock.acquire(lockPath):\n    myPath = client.create(lockPath + '/lock-', data=sessionId,\n                           mode=EPHEMERAL_SEQUENTIAL)   # server assigns the number\n\n    while true:\n        children = client.getChildren(lockPath, watch=false)\n        sorted   = sort(children)            # purely numeric on the suffix\n\n        if myPath == sorted[0]:\n            return LockHandle(myPath,\n                              fencingToken=parseSequenceNumber(myPath))\n\n        predecessor = sorted[indexOf(myPath) - 1]   # the ONE node ahead of me\n        watchResult = client.exists(lockPath + '/' + predecessor, watch=true)\n\n        if watchResult is null:\n            continue          # already gone - recheck NOW, do not wait for a\n                              # watch event that will never fire\n\n        waitForWatchEvent()   # ONE-SHOT: fires once, then must be re-set\n        # loop: re-list children, re-check whether I am now lowest",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "acq",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1070,
   "y": 616,
   "width": 599,
   "height": 30,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100027,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700189,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "getChildren -> exists(watch=true) is NOT atomic - two separate round trips - and\nthat is worth stating plainly rather than reaching for a lock to close the gap.",
   "originalText": "getChildren -> exists(watch=true) is NOT atomic - two separate round trips - and\nthat is worth stating plainly rather than reaching for a lock to close the gap.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1070,
   "y": 674,
   "width": 591,
   "height": 90,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100028,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700196,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "It does not need one. The one place atomicity actually matters - assigning each\nwaiter a strictly ordered sequence number - is already pushed down into the\ncoordination service's own write path, the one place that can provide it for\nfree. So the continue-on-null-watch branch is not a workaround for a missing\nlock; it is the correct response to a real, expected race the design already\naccounts for.",
   "originalText": "It does not need one. The one place atomicity actually matters - assigning each\nwaiter a strictly ordered sequence number - is already pushed down into the\ncoordination service's own write path, the one place that can provide it for\nfree. So the continue-on-null-watch branch is not a workaround for a missing\nlock; it is the correct response to a real, expected race the design already\naccounts for.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bn3",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1070,
   "y": 790,
   "width": 606,
   "height": 75,
   "strokeColor": "#b45309",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100029,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700203,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The one place an in-process guard IS worth adding: a LockHandle called from two\nthreads of the SAME client process. That is a single-process reentrancy problem,\nnot a distributed one - a lightweight local guard is the right tool. Do not reach\nfor a distributed coordination primitive to solve a problem entirely within one\nprocess.",
   "originalText": "The one place an in-process guard IS worth adding: a LockHandle called from two\nthreads of the SAME client process. That is a single-process reentrancy problem,\nnot a distributed one - a lightweight local guard is the right tool. Do not reach\nfor a distributed coordination primitive to solve a problem entirely within one\nprocess.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
