  {
   "id": "el",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1628,
   "width": 1026,
   "height": 21,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100057,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700399,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Patterns, named - and one of them explains why this design needed no second server-side mechanism",
   "originalText": "Patterns, named - and one of them explains why this design needed no second server-side mechanism",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "en",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1666,
   "width": 1011,
   "height": 178,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100058,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700406,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Facade / Repository     CoordinationClient hides the raw session and znode wire protocol; DistributedLock, LeaderElection and\n                        MembershipGroup never talk to the network directly\nStrategy                ZkClient and EtcdClient are interchangeable behind one CoordinationClient interface\nObserver, ONE-SHOT      the watch mechanism IS the Observer pattern, deliberately weakened to fire once: subscribe, get\n                        notified a single time, then explicitly re-subscribe. That one choice is what keeps notification\n                        cost proportional to 'watchers active right now' rather than 'every watcher ever registered'.\nState machine           SessionState's one-way EXPIRED transition - a lifecycle as named states with enforced legal\n                        transitions, never a boolean flag\nTemplate method,        LeaderElection and DistributedLock are the SAME sequential-node algorithm with a different\nhiding in plain sight   onBecomeLowest action - hold the lock, versus run as leader. Worth naming explicitly, because it is\n                        the reason this design never needed two separate server-side mechanisms.",
   "originalText": "Facade / Repository     CoordinationClient hides the raw session and znode wire protocol; DistributedLock, LeaderElection and\n                        MembershipGroup never talk to the network directly\nStrategy                ZkClient and EtcdClient are interchangeable behind one CoordinationClient interface\nObserver, ONE-SHOT      the watch mechanism IS the Observer pattern, deliberately weakened to fire once: subscribe, get\n                        notified a single time, then explicitly re-subscribe. That one choice is what keeps notification\n                        cost proportional to 'watchers active right now' rather than 'every watcher ever registered'.\nState machine           SessionState's one-way EXPIRED transition - a lifecycle as named states with enforced legal\n                        transitions, never a boolean flag\nTemplate method,        LeaderElection and DistributedLock are the SAME sequential-node algorithm with a different\nhiding in plain sight   onBecomeLowest action - hold the lock, versus run as leader. Worth naming explicitly, because it is\n                        the reason this design never needed two separate server-side mechanisms.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "en2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1886,
   "width": 1019,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100059,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700413,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "And the recipe generalizes further than 'one lock, one holder' once you are willing to interpret the ordered children list\ndifferently: a READ-WRITE LOCK distinguishes nodes by a read-/write- prefix under the same path, where a writer still waits on\neveryone ahead of it but a reader waits only on the WRITERS ahead of it - so the loop filters sortedChildren by prefix instead\nof taking the single immediate predecessor.",
   "originalText": "And the recipe generalizes further than 'one lock, one holder' once you are willing to interpret the ordered children list\ndifferently: a READ-WRITE LOCK distinguishes nodes by a read-/write- prefix under the same path, where a writer still waits on\neveryone ahead of it but a reader waits only on the WRITERS ahead of it - so the loop filters sortedChildren by prefix instead\nof taking the single immediate predecessor.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  }
